  "id": "Compound::DB00492 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Fosinopril, a common ACE inhibitor, is linked to Slc15a1 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Fosinopril may cause conditions such as Skull Hypoplasia, Oligohydramnios, and Serositis, which are both associated with Captopril, an ACE inhibitor with a similar mechanism of action. Captopril binds to Slc15a1, indicating a direct interaction that could influence cellular function. The shared ancestry of Fosinopril and Captopril with the class Ace Inhibitor and the category Organooxygen Compound further supports a common biological pathway. The integration of these findings implies that the inhibition of Slc15a1 may be a downstream effect of ACE inhibition, potentially impacting cellular transport processes. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact role of Slc15a1 in these conditions remains to be fully elucidated.",
